Honest verdict

This is much more advanced than I initially assumed. You have assembled Gradio, LangGraph, MCP, RhinoCommon, Flask, pyRevit and multimodal LLM input into one working concept.

But describe it accurately:

A locally hosted, context-aware Rhino and Revit automation agent with a Gradio interface, MCP-based tool routing, multimodal input, conversational memory and AI-generated CAD operations. The current reasoning backend uses the Gemini API.

Do not call it “100% local” yet because Gemini inference leaves the machine. Also do not call arbitrary execution “safe” until approval, validation and sandboxing are added.

The concept is strong, bro. The immediate priorities are:

Fix the /execute versus /execute_code mismatch.
Align the response fields.
Add execution approval and safeguards.
Make selection context a first-class MCP tool.
Either implement the local-engine dropdown or remove it temporarily.
